.TH tudiff n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tudiff
.PP
\fBtclutils::tudiff\fR provides small, portable, line based diff tools in pure Tcl.
.SS Load
.CS
package require tclutils::tudiff
.CE
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tudiff::text oldText newText
::tclutils::tudiff::files oldFile newFile
::tclutils::tudiff::unified oldFile newFile ?options?
::tclutils::tudiff::unifiedText oldText newText ?options?
.CE
.PP
\fBtext\fR and \fBfiles\fR return a list of operations:
.CS
{equal line}
{delete line}
{insert line}
.CE
.SS "Line ends: \fB\-eol\fR"
.PP
\fBtext\fR, \fBfiles\fR, \fBunifiedText\fR, \fBunified\fR, \fBcontextText\fR and \fBcontext\fR take \fB\-eol ignore|strict\fR (0.2):
.TS
l l.
value	effect
\fBignore\fR (default)	CRLF, CR and LF count as the same, a missing final newline does not count
\fBstrict\fR	lines are compared with their line end; \fBa\er\en\fR and \fBa\en\fR differ, so does a missing final newline
.TE
.PP
With \fBstrict\fR the ops of \fBtext\fR and \fBfiles\fR keep each line's end (\fB{equal a\en}\fR); \fBunified\fR and \fBcontext\fR show the line without \fB\en\fR (a \fB\er\fR stays) and add \fB\e No newline at end of file\fR as GNU diff does. \fBfiles\fR, \fBunified\fR and \fBcontext\fR also take \fB\-encoding ENC\fR (default: the system encoding). \fBdirectory\fR compares bytes. An unknown \fB\-eol\fR value is an error \fB{TCLUTILS TUDIFF OPTION EOL}\fR.
.SS "Unified diff"
.CS
puts [::tclutils::tudiff::unified old.txt new.txt]
.CE
.PP
Options:
.CS
-fromlabel label
-tolabel label
.CE
.PP
The first implementation intentionally uses a simple LCS based line diff. It is stable and portable, but not yet optimized for very large files.
.SS "Robustness: \fB\-maxcells\fR"
.PP
\fBtudiff\fR currently uses a simple dynamic\-programming LCS table. This is fine for small and medium reference files, but has O(n*m) memory/time behavior. To avoid accidental large\-file blow\-ups, \fBtext\fR, \fBfiles\fR, \fBunifiedText\fR and \fBunified\fR accept \fB\-maxcells\fR:
.CS
::tclutils::tudiff::text $old $new -maxcells 2000000
::tclutils::tudiff::unified old.txt new.txt -maxcells 5000000
.CE
.PP
If the product of old\-line\-count and new\-line\-count exceeds the limit, the command raises an error with error code:
.CS
TCLUTILS TUDIFF TOO_LARGE
.CE
.PP
A future version may add a streaming or patience\-style algorithm for very large files.
.SS "Context and directory diff"
.CS
::tclutils::tudiff::contextText $old $new
::tclutils::tudiff::context old.txt new.txt
::tclutils::tudiff::directory olddir newdir
.CE
.PP
\fBdirectory\fR returns records such as \fBequal\fR, \fBdifferent\fR, \fBonly\-old\fR, and \fBonly\-new\fR.
